# Vinted listings

Use Playwright MCP (`user-playwright`) on the seller's already-logged-in Vinted session. Never ask for or type the password. Cursor's built-in browser is a different session — do not use it for this. If the session is not logged in as the seller, stop and ask the user to log in.

Do not change prices on other live listings.

Post to Vinted **only when a card goes live** — same moment it goes live on Marktplaats, never for a `concept` card or one that's out of stock. This is part of the **Go live / list {card}** flow in `marktplaats-listings.mdc`: do it right after the Marktplaats ad is confirmed and published, not as a separate standalone trigger.

## New listing

**https://www.vinted.nl/items/new**

Reuse the title and photos already drafted for the Marktplaats ad (see `marktplaats-listings.mdc` → Title). The description is the **English** version of the Marktplaats description (see **Description (English)** below) — Vinted gets international traffic, Marktplaats does not.

- **Photos:** same order as Marktplaats — slab front first, slab back second.
- **Title:** same as the Marktplaats title (the title format is already English).
- **Beschrijving:** the English description below — same structure and content as the Dutch Marktplaats one, translated, never a rewrite.
- **Categorie:** Losse ruilkaarten.
- **Merk:** Pokémon.
- **Staat:** Nieuw zonder prijskaartje.
- **Prijs:** the same amount currently shown on the Marktplaats ad (e.g. `€94,99`) — copy it as-is, don't recompute from the shop price. Vinted's shipping-size recommendation sometimes flips to **Middel** on higher prices; always click back to **Klein** regardless of what it suggests.
- **Verzending:** Klein (smallest package size).

**Stop** before publishing — same rule as Marktplaats: tell the user the form is ready and wait for them to check it. Only after they confirm, publish. Copy the resulting item URL (`https://www.vinted.nl/items/{id}`) onto the product's `vintedUrl` field. The shop then shows **View on Vinted** as a secondary link next to the Marktplaats CTA.

**Publishing the record is part of the same task, not a follow-up.** Once the card is live on both marketplaces, immediately edit `app/cms/seed-products.ts`: set `marktplaatsUrl` and `vintedUrl`, remove `concept: true`, and let the dev server sync it (or `npx vite-node scripts/cms-sync.mts --remote --products`). If the user published the listings themselves, ask for the two URLs right away. Never end the task with a live card still marked `concept` — Pikachu (September 2026) and Mega Gardevoir ex (September 2026) were both left as concepts and the user had to point it out. `scripts/hooks/listing-publish-check.mjs` (wired in `.claude/settings.json`) warns when a concept product already has a branded ad photo in `public/ads`.

## Description (English)

Same structure, sections, bold and blank lines as the Marktplaats description (`marktplaats-listings.mdc` → Description), translated one-to-one. Draft the Dutch Marktplaats description first, then translate it — do not add or drop anything. Same pop rule: only mention pop when it is low; skip subgrades / graded date / pop when we do not have them. Never a cert number.

Vinted's description field is a plain textarea, so bold is not rendered — type the text without the `**` markers, keep the blank lines between sections and the `•` bullets.

